; The N163 has up to eight wave channels, but they take turns: the highest
; one named sets how many run, and the more run, the quieter each and the
; louder the chip's whine. Past five they share the wave memory too, so a
; wave plays every other step (the compiler says so).
; Try: add n163-wave8 and hear the whine.
(def-score :target fc)
(def-wave saw :wave (saw -128..127))
(n163-wave1 saw :len 2 c g)
